Sure, but my feeling is that while those give you
the "hard" information (things that won't change
in the game), the mails actually allow you to
convey last minute impressions and
thoughts to give the next person the state
of mind you're in.  I think this is more useful
later on.  Assume you get a game at the castle.
Getting a message like "I'm trying to get more
xp to go on the quest" or "watch out for the
black dragon in the closet" is useful...

Also, it turns out that you can write multiple
lines of mail on a single scroll <more>
which allows me to write a whole essay on
a single scroll rather than (possibly confusing)
one liners on various items.

